course: dictionary
lesson: 13903
title: Lapsed: ending and slipping
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word lapsed can mean that something has come to an end because it was not renewed in time. «My library card has lapsed, so I cannot borrow books until I renew it.» The clue is not renewed in time, so lapsed means it has run out.
explain: A lapsed member is someone who used to belong to a club but no longer does. «Mia is a lapsed member of the chess club.» The clue is used to belong: she is not in the club now.
explain: Lapsed into is different. It means slowly slipped into a state. «When the music stopped, the hall lapsed into silence.» Ask: what word would fit here? Slowly became silent fits, so that is the meaning.
fact: Lapsed is the past form of the verb lapse.
fact: «Lapsed» can describe something that has come to an end because it was not renewed in time, like a card or a membership.
fact: A lapsed member or believer used to belong or believe, but no longer does.
fact: «Lapsed into» means slowly slipped into a state, as in «lapsed into silence».
fact: A good check is to swap in a simple word, such as ended or slowly became, and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «My library card has lapsed, because I did not renew it.» What does lapsed mean here? | Has been lost in the rain | *Has run out, because it was not renewed in time | Has been painted bright red | Has grown very large
exercise: «Mia is a lapsed member of the chess club.» What does lapsed member suggest? | *Someone who used to belong to the club but no longer does | Someone who never plays chess | A member who is very old | Someone who has just won a chess game
exercise: «When the music stopped, the hall lapsed into silence.» What does lapsed into silence mean? | *Slowly became silent | Ran out of the hall | Shouted very loudly | Began to sing a song
test: «After three years, Dad's insurance lapsed.» What does lapsed mean here? | Was sent to a new address | *Ended because it was not renewed in time | Became much cheaper | Grew stronger
test: «The noise lapsed into a soft hum, then stopped.» What does lapsed into mean? | *Slowly slipped into a state | Jumped suddenly | Went out for lunch | Came back again
exam: In «his membership lapsed last month», which word means the same as lapsed? | counted | started | painted | *ended
